# Auto-commit and push (daily-driver fork)

After every coherent code, docs, or template change in this repo:

1. Create a signed commit with `git commit -s` and
   `type(scope): imperative summary`. Do not wait for the user to ask.
2. Push to the `fork` remote on the current branch (`git push fork HEAD`).
3. Keep unrelated dirty work in separate commits when practical.
4. Never commit `.garbage/`, credentials, profile databases, private logs,
   runtime artifacts, or generated `target/` output.

This project preference overrides the generic Cursor default that only
commits when explicitly asked.
